            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "gapch1026"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had a can of creamed corn in my pantry. So I scaled this recipe to half and used only 1 Tblsp flour and 2 cups 2% milk. I thought that the addition of the creamed corn gave it the perfect chowder creaminess. Added a bit of chipotle powder and cumin as suggested by a reviewer, and some real bacon bits. The popcorn was a fun garnish! I'll make this soup again with my changes."
          },
          {
